cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "statespace-toolkit: MATLAB code for Bayesian state space models"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the paper whose method you use
  (see the Citation section of README.md) and this software record.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chan
    given-names: Joshua C. C.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3632-128X"
    affiliation: Purdue University
repository-code: "https://github.com/joshuaccchan/statespace-toolkit"
url: "https://joshuachan.org/code.html"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB code for Bayesian state space models. A tested library holds the
  building blocks of their samplers: the precision sampler, which draws a whole
  state path from the banded precision matrix of the states, the integrated
  likelihood, the treatment of missing data and of data at mixed frequencies,
  and an accept-reject Metropolis-Hastings step for states whose conditional
  distribution is not Gaussian. Eight examples use them in complete samplers,
  among them unobserved components, time-varying parameter, dynamic factor,
  stochastic volatility in mean and TVP-MIDAS models. The repository also
  archives fourteen replication packages, each archived file byte for byte as
  published, and unit tests check the library against the published code it
  replaces.
keywords:
  - Bayesian econometrics
  - state space models
  - precision sampler
  - Markov chain Monte Carlo
  - unobserved components
  - stochastic volatility
  - time-varying parameters
  - missing data
  - MATLAB
